    keywords:"binance belgium, binance fsma, binance banned belgium, binance alternative belgium, crypto exchange belgium, beste crypto exchange belgië, binance mica, crypto futures belgium",
    faq:[{"q":"Did Belgium ban Binance?","a":"In 2023 Belgium's financial regulator, the FSMA, ordered Binance to cease offering certain virtual-currency services in the country from entities based outside the EEA. It was a restriction on specific services rather than a simple blanket ban, and the EU picture has shifted since under MiCA. Check the current status for Belgium before acting — this is general information, not advice."},{"q":"What can Belgian traders use instead of Binance?","a":"Belgian traders commonly compare Bybit, OKX, KuCoin, Gate and Kraken. The right choice depends on fees, liquidity, leverage and whether the platform serves Belgian residents and is MiCA-compliant. See our best crypto futures exchanges guide and confirm availability before depositing."},{"q":"Is crypto trading legal in Belgium?","a":"Yes — owning and trading crypto is legal in Belgium. The FSMA regulates how services are offered and has acted against specific non-compliant offerings. As always, use a platform that legally serves Belgium and verify the current rules. Not financial or legal advice."}],
    body:"    <p>Trading from Belgium and wondering where Binance stands? In <strong>2023 the FSMA</strong> — Belgium's financial regulator — <strong>ordered Binance to stop offering certain crypto services</strong> in the country. Here's what that actually meant, what <strong>MiCA</strong> changed, and the <strong>alternatives</strong> Belgian traders use. <em>(General information, not financial or legal advice — verify the current rules for your situation.)</em></p>\n    <h2>What happened with Binance in Belgium</h2>\n    <p>In <strong>June 2023</strong>, the <strong>FSMA (Financial Services and Markets Authority)</strong> ordered Binance to <strong>cease offering certain virtual-currency services in Belgium</strong> that were being provided from <strong>entities based outside the European Economic Area (EEA)</strong>. It was a restriction on <strong>how and from where</strong> services could be offered — not a simple \"crypto is illegal\" ban — but the practical effect was that some Belgian users lost access to parts of the platform. It was part of the same 2023 wave that saw Binance <a href=\"/blog/binance-alternatives-netherlands/\">leave the Netherlands</a>; see the full <a href=\"/blog/is-binance-banned-in-europe/\">Binance in Europe overview</a>.</p>\n    <h2>What MiCA changed</h2>\n    <p>Since 2023, the EU's <strong>MiCA</strong> regulation has phased in across <strong>2024&ndash;2025</strong>, creating a <strong>single EU-wide licensing regime</strong> that passports across member states — Belgium included. That has reshaped the picture, so don't rely on the 2023 status: <strong>check the current availability</strong> of any exchange for Belgium before you act.</p>\n    <h2>Best alternatives for Belgian traders</h2>\n    <p>Whether or not Binance fully serves you, these are the venues Belgian traders most often compare:</p>\n    <ul>\n    <li><strong>Bybit</strong> — deep perpetual-futures liquidity.</li>\n    <li><strong>OKX</strong> — broad markets and competitive fees.</li>\n    <li><strong>KuCoin</strong> — wide altcoin range.</li>\n    <li><strong>Gate</strong> — huge selection of perpetual pairs.</li>\n    <li><strong>Kraken</strong> — long-established and regulation-facing.</li>\n    </ul>\n    <p>They differ on fees, leverage, liquidity and Belgian availability. Our <a href=\"/blog/best-crypto-futures-exchanges/\">best crypto futures exchanges</a> guide explains how to choose, and you can <strong>compare them on our exchanges page</strong>. Always confirm the platform <strong>serves Belgian residents and is MiCA-compliant</strong> before funding in EUR.</p>\n    <h2>Learn leverage free first</h2>\n    <p>Before you deposit anywhere, make sure you understand the mechanics. Run trades on our free <a href=\"/paper-trade\">Paper Trade terminal</a> at the live price — no money, no account — and watch your <a href=\"/#liq\">liquidation line</a> move as you change leverage. Then <a href=\"/screener\">scan the live perp markets</a> to compare funding and volatility before you commit.</p>\n    <div class=\"callout\"><div class=\"k\">COMPARE EXCHANGES</div><p style=\"margin-bottom:14px\">Binance restricted in Belgium? Compare the leading alternatives on fees, leverage and availability, and pick one that serves Belgium.</p><a class=\"cta\" href=\"/#exchanges\">See the exchanges &rarr;</a></div>"
